## Workflow

- Create a plan first. Show me the plan in digestible chunks and wait for my "go" before applying it.
- Always use **zsh**. Source `~/.zshrc` before running commands so the environment matches my interactive terminal.
- **Never run any git command on your own — always ask and confirm first.** Covers commit, push, checkout, rebase, and merge.
- When tests fail, show me only the errors — filter console output, don't dump it raw.
- Always run lint to fix files before finishing an implementation.
- Temporary-file cleanup period: 15 days.

## Package Manager & Monorepo Paths

- Always check which package manager the project uses first — start with `pnpm`.
- For workspace/monorepo commands, the path is relative to the package, not the repo root.
  e.g. `pnpm --filter @gorgias-chat/client test:unit src/foo/Bar.spec.tsx`

## Superpowers Persistence

- Persist ALL Superpowers artifacts (brainstorming notes, plans, design docs, skill outputs)
  under `/Users/guilhermebomfim/developer/gorgias-power-project/<repo>/superpowers/`, where
  `<repo>` is the repo currently being worked on.
- Never write these artifacts into the repo itself — always centralize under the path above.
- Before brainstorming, planning, or resuming work, check that path for existing artifacts and use them as context.
- Combine the repo (code, docs) WITH the centralized artifacts — read both together.

